00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.200
So let's start with what
Smart Arts actually are.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.710
According to the Office support page,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.697
Smart Arts are something that you can use

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:39.227
"to quickly and easily make a visual

00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:41.487
"representation of your information.

00:01:41.487 --> 00:01:44.057
"You can choose among
many different layouts

00:01:44.057 --> 00:01:46.537
"to efficiently or effectively communicate

00:01:46.537 --> 00:01:48.180
"your message or idea."

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.960
So basically, Smart Arts is something

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.720
that Microsoft invented with
the intention to help you

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.750
to quickly and easily
visualize your information.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.790
So let's look at a few
examples, just that you

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.460
get an idea of what I'm talking about.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.520
So Smart Arts, you can
find here under Insert,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.300
and then Smart Arts, and then here,

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.010
a whole menu of different things opens up.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.810
And on first sight, it looks quite

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.130
helpful and interesting, right?

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.660
These are different examples
of things you can use,

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.603
of forms and shapes that
might be, indeed, helpful

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:20.950
in order to visualize your ideas.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.980
So let's just open a few, for instance,

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.470
something like this,
little boxes with text.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.270
Apparently you could put
photos in here as well.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.860
Let's make it a little bit smaller.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.403
Maybe another one, something
like this looks interesting,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.350
or even another example,
maybe here in a matrix,

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.290
such an assembly of different squares

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.830
where you can also put text in it.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.270
So, yes, I agree, on first sight,

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.690
it looks interesting and
helpful, and actually,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.340
Smart Arts I personally see
being used quite frequently

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.200
in amateur presentations,
and people who are not

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.590
really using PowerPoint frequently

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.880
or not using PowerPoint in
any professional capacity,

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.650
in these kind of presentations,

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.480
I see Smart Arts frequently used.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.180
But, now, it might surprise you that in

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.210
professional presentations,
in presentations

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.460
that are being done in big,
large, blue-chip companies,

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.700
and especially by large
strategy consulting firms,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.520
Smart Arts are literally never used.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.760
People just do not use Smart Arts.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.500
In this video, I'd like to go over

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.500
the advantages and
mainly the disadvantages

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.170
of using Smart Arts to help you understand

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.710
why people actually don't use Smart Arts,

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.720
and why it's just really bad to use them,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.840
and I will also show a few alternatives

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.600
of what you actually can do in order to do

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.170
very similar things,
pretty much get the same

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.880
results without actually using
Smart Arts in PowerPoint.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.320
So, now, let's look into something

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.800
that you will frequently use in management

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.920
presentations, and this
is some visualization

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.650
of a process chart.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.710
So here, I now created
kind of a basic template

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.530
of how this could look like.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.050
So you see, now, a collection
of different steps,

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:10.040
step one, step two, step
three, step four, step five.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.200
It's a process, so
these steps are supposed

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.827
to happen one after each
other, and now you'd like

00:04:14.827 --> 00:04:17.490
to visualize it and also give details

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.180
on the individual steps with some kind of

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.150
hierarchy of bullet points.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.350
And this is really a typical chart

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.110
that you would use in consulting.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.580
In my six years at McKinsey, I used charts

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.390
like that many, many times.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.550
I probably created over 100 of pages

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.440
that look more or less
like this, of course,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.440
without some variations,
how many steps are included,

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.970
or how exactly it is
shown, but pretty much

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:47.030
pages like that are very
commonly used in consulting.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.670
And from the style, you would think

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.870
that this is something that you probably

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.310
could do really well with a Smart Art.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.530
I mean, after all, Smart Arts are exactly

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:56.960
supposed to help you do things like that,

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.610
help you create charts like that where you

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.890
can easily display and visualize
your information, right?

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.370
So, well, let's try to
create a page like that

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.040
or somehow similar like
that in a Smart Art.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.460
So first, we need to
choose a suitable design.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.550
So let's go into Smart
Arts, and here you see

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.620
that they actually have a whole section

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.530
of how to visualize processes, so, indeed,

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.890
Smart Arts apparently are exactly supposed

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.810
to help you visualize process like that.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.100
And from my perspective, now, we chose

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:34.100
a very basic form, maybe a process chart

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.100
where at the top, you
see the different steps,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.810
and then you have some text
below to describe them.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.890
But now, here, if we go over the designs,

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.650
actually, most of the designs are supposed

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.510
to look much more fancy,
much more complicated,

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.680
where there are lots of different
shapes and relationships,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.030
but such a very basic
shape, where you just have

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:59.010
a header and then text to describe it,

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.500
is not really included here.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.820
Probably the closest
thing that you can find

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.360
is this one, where you have
a header giving a title

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.510
of the different steps, and
then some space to explain them.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.300
And this is something,
the first thing that I see

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.640
a lot when looking at
Smart Arts, that their

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.480
designs that they have are
often not very practical.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.770
They are much more playful
than actually useful,

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:28.167
because most of the time, charts like that

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.930
are not really helpful
in use, but you need

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.930
more simpler things, which then you aren't

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.370
even able to do in the Smart Art.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.920
But let's now pick this design,

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:39.080
because apparently, this is what Microsoft

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.220
thinks you should use when you create

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.080
such a process approach, where you have

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.060
different steps and then text explaining

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.450
the details on the step.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.250
So first of all, let's try to do some

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.650
basic formatting on it.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.750
Let's try to set a font size of 14.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.160
And the first thing that you notice

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.797
when I changed the font
size, that pretty much

00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:05.350
the whole dimension of all
these different objects changed.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.280
So usually, you would
expect that if you changed

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.693
the font size, pretty much
everything stays the same,

00:07:09.693 --> 00:07:12.990
only the font size changes,
but here, it's not the case.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.760
And you will not see it, but this is one

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.410
of the reasons that it's
pretty difficult to actually

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.600
work with Smart Arts,
because one little change

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.220
that you do to one little
part of the Smart Art

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:26.191
very frequently changes
the whole Smart Art.

00:07:26.191 --> 00:07:28.280
It just really makes it difficult

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.820
in getting the exact result that you want.

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:31.790
But let's continue working.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:35.350
Now, we had, not three
steps, as we see here,

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.910
but actually five steps, so let's now

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.440
include additional steps.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.330
Now we have the five steps here.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.010
Let's now try to drag it in a way

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:47.730
that the whole page is covered,

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.683
so that you don't waste space.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.040
And let's now try to use similar text

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.170
as we had on our example page.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.880
Now, lazy people like me could think

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.520
that you might be able to just copy that

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:07.410
in here, but for whatever reason, that

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.220
just doesn't really seem to work right.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.880
So if I call this First Aspect,

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.300
and now, please tell me, for what reason

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.220
is this now smaller than the rest?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.530
Also, if you look here into
the hierarchy of bullets,

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.740
it looks exactly the way that here,

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.470
but for whatever reason now, with the

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.233
Smart Art, reduced the font size.

00:08:24.233 --> 00:08:28.543
So now you can go back
and put it back to 14.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.240
I think you get the idea.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.130
Let's now just imagine that you have had

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.500
all the text here that you wanted,

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.450
but now, what you can see is the design,

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.520
as it's used here, it's
not very efficiently

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:46.520
using the space, because
you see lots of blank space.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:48.880
So what we actually would need to do now,

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.190
especially if you compare
it with this style graph,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.389
where I could not easily fit lots of text,

00:08:53.389 --> 00:08:56.381
we need to make these
little boxes a bit larger

00:08:56.381 --> 00:09:00.170
in order to actually create more space.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.620
So usually I would now
highlight all the boxes

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:07.360
and then try to drag them a bit larger

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.230
in a way that then I have more space.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.660
And now, we see it
again, I have now dragged

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.090
the boxes a bit larger,
and for whatever reason,

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.180
now this upper part is now much smaller

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.150
and looks much different.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.730
Okay, so now I could
highlight probably these,

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.540
'cause also, this is now
a super-large surface,

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.480
given that it's covered by the extra text,

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:28.820
so why would you need that?

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.493
So let's now make it smaller.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.710
And you can see here
that it's automatically,

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.050
I'm not holding any keys, trying to make

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.630
the upper part smaller as well.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.730
So if I release, now it looks like this,

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.620
which of course doesn't
make sense, so I go back.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.120
So, tell me, now, what do I need to do

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.360
in order to make these things smaller?

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:52.690
If I now handle one,
it now looks like this.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.468
So just extremely
difficult, now, to get it

00:09:55.468 --> 00:09:56.960
in a way that I want to.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:01.283
Maybe now I can try to
shift all of them a bit up.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.093
Now if I do that, maybe
I'll have a bit more luck.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.920
You see that it's just extremely

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.520
difficult to work with that, right?

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.190
Okay, but now we can tell ourself

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:14.920
that maybe we just chose
the wrong Smart Art.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.710
Maybe there's another Smart Art type

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:20.370
that is actually much easier to use.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.150
Let's go back into
Process, and the one thing

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.930
that I saw a bit earlier that probably

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.050
would help me to get such an effect

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:34.050
is one of these process arts, right?

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:35.740
So let's try them out.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.510
This now would be an alternative

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.150
where you can put some text under it.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:44.740
So now, again, let's try to fill it

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.800
